/*
 * Declares the PrototypeValue class.
 *
 * PrototypeValue represents the generator-level form of a callable function
 * prototype. It captures the full signature of a function — its symbol,
 * parameters, return type, attributes, and the module in which it is defined —
 * without representing an actual invocation.
 *
 * PrototypeValue is used throughout the generator and template-rewriting
 * pipeline to:
 *   - describe callable entities in a uniform way,
 *   - support template specialization and template-rewriter scoring,
 *   - expose attributes such as `unsafe` and `inline`,
 *   - provide access to parameter and return-type information,
 *   - preserve the origin module for diagnostics and linking.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::prototypes::basic
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/prototypes/basic.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-02-27
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
